==Etymology==
Upchuck's name is a pun of the verb "upchuck", which means to vomit, referencing his abilities.

The Perk prefix is named after [[Thomas N. Perkins IV]], who designed Upchuck's appearance in the '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]'''.{{Refn|[[:File:Perk Gourmand Name Reference.png]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:Perk and Murk Namesakes.png]]|group = DJW|name = namesakes}}{{Refn|[[:File:Tom Designed S3 & S4 Characters.png]]|group = TNP|name = tom}}

The Murk prefix is named after [[Glen Murakami]], who redesigned Upchuck for '''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (TV Series)|Alien Force]]''' and '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]'''.{{Refn|[[:File:Murk Gourmand Name Reference.png]]|group = TNP}}{{Refn|group = DJW|name = namesakes}}

==Trivia==
*Murk Upchuck's appearance in ''[[Vengeance of Vilgax: Part 2]]'' was the first mistransformation in '''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (TV Series)|Alien Force]]'''.
*Like [[Arctiguana]], [[Buzzshock (Classic)|Buzzshock]], [[Frankenstrike]], and [[Snare-Oh]], Murk Upchuck appeared in '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''', but he did not appear in ''[[A New Dawn]]''.
**The out-of-universe reason Murk Upchuck had fewer appearances than Perk Upchuck in '''Omniverse''' is because [[Derrick J. Wyatt]] believed "Perks are the best Upchucks".{{Refn|[[:File:DJW Prefers Perk.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Upchuck is one of the five aliens who have appeared in every series in the Classic Continuity; the other four are [[Cannonbolt (Classic)|Cannonbolt]], [[Diamondhead (Classic)|Diamondhead]], [[Way Big (Classic)|Way Big]], and [[Ghostfreak]].
*Murk Upchuck is the first alien in '''Alien Force''' to not have the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] on his chest. Instead, the symbol was on his stomach.
*Perk Upchuck and [[Bullfrag]] are the only aliens to have been manually unlocked by entering a code into an [[Omnitrix]].
*In every video game that Upchuck appears in, he is exclusive to the DS and/or 3DS versions.
*Although Murk Upchuck only appeared twice in '''Omniverse''', a toy for him was made. Derrick told [[Cartoon Network]] consumer products that they were making a toy for the wrong Upchuck, but they said it was too far along to change.{{Refn|[[:File:DJW Told CN Consumer Products They Were Making the Wrong Upchuck Toy.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Upchuck is the only known Omnitrix alien who can switch between the different races of his species.<ref name="TT" />{{Refn|[[:File:Upchuck Can Switch Between Subspecies.PNG]]|group = DJW}} Azmuth's reasons for including both subspecies are unknown.{{Refn|[[:File:Upchuck Subspecies Special.PNG]]|group = DJW}}
**The out-of-universe reason for this is because Derrick liked both of Upchuck's designs, even though he preferred Perks, and wanted to use them together on the show.{{Refn|[[:File:Derrick Prefers Perks.PNG]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:DJW Wanted to Use Both Upchuck Subspecies.png]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:DJW Wanted to Use Both Upchuck Subspecies 2.PNG]]|group = DJW}}
*Upchuck would have been the real winner of the loogie contest in ''[[Back With a Vengeance]]'' had [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] unlocked him prior to the events of the episode.{{Refn|[[:File:Upchuck Spitting Contest Winner.png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref>''[[Back With a Vengeance]]''</ref>
*Upchuck's '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]''' design was made by [[Thomas N. Perkins IV]],{{Refn|group = TNP|name = tom}} who envisioned him as a vaguely humanoid amoeba-like creature. He was always supposed to be translucent,{{Refn|[[:File:Upchuck Supposed to Be Translucent.png]]|group = TNP}} and had a translucent tummy, but since that detail did not appear in the series, fans have mistaken him to be a humanoid frog/toad.{{Refn|group = TNP|name = amoeba}}
**Thomas designed Perk Upchuck with three tongues, but he is commonly depicted with four tongues, in the series and official artwork, and on his battle version toy.{{Refn|group = TNP|name = tongue}} He is also described as having four tongues on his bio on the [[Cartoon Network]] website{{Refn|[[:File:Upchuck CN Site.png]]|group = CN|name = network}} and the ''Ben 10 Alien Force: Volume 6'' DVD.{{Refn|group = DVD|name = af dvd}}
**Upchuck's '''Omniverse''' designs were created by Derrick.{{Refn|[[:File:Some of the Aliens Designed by Derrick in OV.png]]|group = DJW}} Unlike most aliens featured in '''Omniverse''' that had clothes in the '''Original Series''', Perk Upchuck was unclothed as Derrick thought he appeared cuter and more uncivilized naked.{{Refn|[[:File:Why Upchuck Has No Clothes.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Some of Perk Upchuck's concept designs were used to create [[Spitter]], Arctiguana, [[Sploot]], [[Mot Snikrep]], and [[Zzzakt]].{{Refn|[[:File:Upchuck Concept Art Tom Perkins.png]]|group = TNP|name = Upchuck}}
*Murk Upchuck was originally not supposed to appear in the dream in ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]''.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/d/d4/Night_of_the_Living_Nightmare_Script_First_Draft.pdf ''Night of the Living Nightmare'' Script First Draft]|group = script|name = first}}

